{"id": "EUVD-2026-108842", "enisaUuid": "3c2e7a56-349e-3967-8fee-bf9aa75dba49", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngve: fix XSK buffer leak when rings are stopped\n\nGVE does not free XSK buffers when resetting ring state as a part of\nstopping queues. This causes all XSK buffers which are posted to the\nNIC to be leaked.\n\nFree XSK buffers attached to an allocated buf_state when stopping rings.\n\nThis issue was hit in production.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/506f9de069d07a72b9887ce3edd2fdf32f4953aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a7e6bbbf0586c1f62f0cc7d9a2877d8a5e5aaf7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/73670ddb91a4d22e1deb3efd962242de1ec48e90"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99047"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1ee8e463-9a3e-348a-86e1-e1ac26b22fcf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c1fffc5d66a7147d557736c2341a511e0896d9ff <506f9de069d07a72b9887ce3edd2fdf32f4953aa"}, {"id": "39c79908-6bea-361e-a57f-09ca53815c3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "569876cb-7318-3b41-b375-281fa8cd8108", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "98cede7d-b86e-3d24-8fd5-dce2ac8b72ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "e82abcd2-70fb-3966-ae07-88bd3bc8488b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c1fffc5d66a7147d557736c2341a511e0896d9ff <7a7e6bbbf0586c1f62f0cc7d9a2877d8a5e5aaf7"}, {"id": "ea9fc99c-c9e4-3fbb-984e-0b3d87ce78ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f31c3972-3637-3834-a6ac-d84219af3692", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, 